    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change is implemented in `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel()` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`).\n\n**What changed:** Added a level-4 factor gated on tenure. The level now starts at 1, gains +1 for an email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`, and now **+1 when tenure exceeds 365 days** \u2014 computed as `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365` \u2014 capped at 4 (was 3).\n\n**Why a new owner stays at level 3:** `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate` sets a new owner's `registrationDate` to today, so tenure is 0, which is not `> 365`. The tenure factor never applies at creation, so a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount == 0` (and a 3-member household) lands at level 3, never 4 \u2014 exactly what the `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` test asserts.\n\n**Tests:** `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green (including the new acceptance test).",
